# The nightly's failure path (ADR 0054): cairn-nightly.service names this unit in `OnFailure=`, so a
# failed night asks the running brain, on loopback, to push "the nightly judges failed" to every
# subscribed device, naming where the log is. The route (`POST /_cairn/notify/nightly-failed`,
# apps/server/src/push/NightlyFailedRoute.ts) takes no body and answers only a process on this host.
# It answers 502 when no device took the push, and this unit then fails, so `systemctl --user
# --failed` still shows the night. A brain that is down cannot push; the nightly's own unit status
# and ~/cairn-judges/ still hold the verdict. The port is cairn.service's (3774).
# Linked into ~/.config/systemd/user by ops/cairn/install.sh.
[Unit]
Description=Cairn nightly failed: push it to the user's devices

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/curl --silent --show-error --fail-with-body --max-time 60 --request POST http://127.0.0.1:3774/_cairn/notify/nightly-failed
